 Why this build exists
 ---------------------
-v0.9 ReadProof proved the read was clean but revealed the real fault: the
-analyzer was latching the WRONG draw. The v0.9 run reported:
-  Source-proof sample: tex 14, 512 x 512   (a probe-space specular)
-  source read: OK, componentType UNSIGNED_NORMALIZED, redBits 8
-  source + CENTER all 0.0%
-while the actual main-pass specularRect sat right there as tex 8, 3840 x 2027.
-
-Firestorm issues several authoritative probe draws per frame at the SAME
-refmapCount: small 512x512 probe-space deferred passes and the full-resolution
-main deferred pass. refmapCount cannot tell them apart. We were freezing and
-analyzing whichever came first, which was a 512x512 probe pass -- so every
-"zero" so far was a clean read of the wrong, empty probe texture.
-
-What changed (add-on only; FX unchanged)
------------------------------------------
-v0.10 gates the specular freeze/analyze to the full-resolution MAIN deferred
-pass. It tracks the tallest specular draw seen and only freezes/analyzes draws
-at >= 75% of that height, so 512-tall probe passes are rejected and the full-res
-main pass (e.g. 2027 tall) is accepted. The gate self-calibrates to the runtime
-resolution -- nothing is hardcoded. Only the source-proof freeze/analyze path is
-gated; the rest of probe selection is untouched.
-
-New overlay line:
-  Specular main-pass gate: max specular height N, last gated height N
-The existing "Source-proof sample: tex .., W x H" line is the proof: it must now
-read the full-res main pass (e.g. 3840 x 2027 / tex 8), not 512 x 512.
-
-Install (native add-on -> Firestorm CLOSED)
---------------------------------------------
-Close Firestorm, run SL_InstallLatest.ps1. Confirm overlay title reads
-"SL Probe Lighting v1.6.8 ... (v0.10 MainPassGate)".
-
-Test target: LEGACY / Blinn-Phong with real specular COLOUR
-------------------------------------------------------------
-Same as before: a legacy object with an actual specular tint or specular map
-(not merely glossiness), filling the centre and a large part of the frame.
+v0.10 MainPassGate proved the source and copy path:
+  - full-resolution main-pass specularRect selected (3840 x 2027 in the proven run)
+  - clean RGBA8 read
+  - nonzero center RGB
+  - private snapshot matched source
+
+That closed acquisition. But v0.10 still published SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR by preferring
+current/last live specular capture before the proven snapshot. The live capture is
+still selected by the older probe-candidate logic, where refmapCount alone cannot
+separate the 512x512 probe-space pass from the full-resolution main pass.
+
+What changed
+------------
+Only the consumer/source priority changes:
+  1. GATED MAIN-PASS SNAPSHOT is now authoritative for SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR.
+  2. DIRECT current/last Firestorm attachment is fallback only.
+  3. The overlay exposes the actual FX source near the existing snapshot line.
+
+The SSR weighting algorithm is intentionally NOT changed in this build. This keeps
+v0.11 a single proof: does the FX consume the same main-pass material payload that
+v0.10 already proved numerically?
+
+Install
+-------
+Native add-on package. Close Firestorm, then run SL_InstallLatest.ps1.
+Confirm the overlay title reads:
+  SL Probe Lighting v1.6.9 ... (v0.11 MainPassConsume)
 
