-======================================
+SL SSR v0.11 MainPassConsume -- interpret
+=========================================
 
-First, confirm the gate worked
-------------------------------
-Look at "Source-proof sample: tex .., W x H".
-  - If it now shows the full-res main pass (e.g. tex 8, 3840 x 2027): GATE OK.
-    Proceed to the decision tree below.
-  - If it STILL shows 512 x 512: the gate did not select the main pass. Send the
-    "Specular main-pass gate: max height / last gated height" line. If max height
-    is 512, no full-res specular draw was seen this session (the main pass isn't
-    being matched by inspect_probe_draw) -> next build widens draw matching, not
-    the gate. If max height is ~2027 but last gated is 512, the threshold logic
-    is wrong -> tell me and I fix the ratio.
-
-Decision tree (once the sample is the full-res main pass)
----------------------------------------------------------
-Target = legacy object with real specular colour, filling centre.
-
-A. source read: FAILED or glError != 0
-   -> read path problem on the full-res texture; report componentType. (Unlikely
-      now; v0.9 already read tex 8 cleanly.)
-
-B. read OK, source/CENTER RGB nonzero
-   -> The authoritative main-pass specularRect has real specular colour where the
-      object is. CAPTURE IS FINALLY PROVEN. The v0.8 gating question is closed.
-      Any remaining black reflection is downstream (FX binding / weighting), not
-      G-buffer acquisition -> resume SSR appearance work.
-
-C. read OK, CENTER RGB == 0 but CENTER A (gloss) nonzero
-   -> This specific material has glossiness but no specular colour. Re-test with a
-      material that definitely has a specular tint/map. If a KNOWN-tinted material
-      still reads RGB 0 on the full-res main pass, that is a real material-contract
-      bug -> next build re-examines the specularRect binding at the main draw.
-
-D. read OK, CENTER all four channels == 0 on the full-res main pass
-   -> The full-res specularRect is empty where a lit object is. Either the object
-      still isn't covering the centre block, or the main soften pass reads
-      specularRect from a different unit than we captured. Confirm coverage; if
-      still zero, next build re-reads the sampler binding at the gated draw.
-
-Notes
------
-- Snapshot lines should now also reflect the full-res main pass (the snapshot is
-  gated by the same path). If snapshot is still 512 x 512 while source is full-res
-  it means the snapshot latched before the gate calibrated -- hold the scene a few
-  seconds and re-click Analyze.
-- Legacy only. Do not switch to PBR to force nonzero.
-- No appearance tuning until branch B.
+Purpose
+-------
+Prove downstream consumption, not acquisition.
+
+Expected overlay
+----------------
+  SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR FX source: GATED MAIN-PASS SNAPSHOT
+
+If it says GATED MAIN-PASS SNAPSHOT:
+  The FX semantic is consuming the source whose bytes v0.10 already proved.
+  Then inspect Display Mode -> G-buffer specular RGB on the same object.
+
+If it says DIRECT FALLBACK (UNGATED):
+  Snapshot timing/publication missed begin_effects. Do not tune SSR. Fix the
+  snapshot publication lifetime first.
+
+If it says NONE:
+  Semantic publication failed. Do not tune SSR.
+
+Expected FX diagnostic
+----------------------
+Display Mode -> G-buffer specular RGB should visibly contain the material payload
+on the known specular test object rather than an empty/black 512x512 probe payload.
+
+After this passes
+-----------------
+Move to legacy SSR response/weighting. The current v0.8-era FX still gates legacy
+reflection through specularRect.a glossiness; Firestorm's pinned native SSR post
+shader instead multiplies reflected RGB by legacy specularRect.rgb directly. That
+known algorithm mismatch is deliberately left for the next revision so this test
+has one variable.
